-- title:
--   Finiteness along β̄ for prime level increase ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $N$ be a natural number that is nonzero, and let $\ell$ be a prime. Write $F^{\mathrm{full}}_M$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull M`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the set `divisorExpansions M`, and write $L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_M$ for `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull M)`, the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image of $F^{\mathrm{full}}_M$ under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb L` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ into $L((q))$. The map `heckeBetaBar L N ℓ` is the $L$-algebra homomorphism $L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_N \to L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_{N\ell}$ induced by `qExpand L ℓ`, the ring endomorphism of $L((q))$ that multiplies all exponents by $\ell$ (substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$), together with the fact that this substitution carries the level-$N$ field into the level-$N\ell$ field. The assertion is [`AlgebraicCurve.FiniteAlong L (ModularCurve.heckeBetaBar L N ℓ)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_Correspondence.html#L37): with respect to the algebra structure on $L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_{N\ell}$ over $L\cdot F^{\mathrm{full}}_N$ transported along this homomorphism, the larger field is a finite module over the smaller one.
--
--   This is the finiteness of the second (degeneracy) embedding in the pair of maps underlying the Hecke correspondence at prime level $\ell$ on the modular function fields, stated unconditionally for prime $\ell$; classically it is the statement that $j(q)$ is integral of finite degree over the field generated by the $j(q^{d})$ at level $N\ell$ pulled back by $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$. It is one of the standing finiteness inputs for the construction and analysis of the Hecke correspondence on $\mathrm{Pic}^{0}$ and for the ramification and place-prolongation computations that use it.
